, including nutritional deficiencies and increased morbidity. [Data: Entities (2284), Relationships (3103, 6792)]\n\n## Pilocarpina's effectiveness in alleviating dry mouth\n\nPilocarpina is specifically designed to treat xerostomia, which can severely impact a patient's ability to eat and maintain proper nutrition. Administered at doses of 5-10 mg every 8 hours, it can help stimulate saliva production, thereby improving the patient's quality of life. The systemic effects of Pilocarpina, while beneficial, may also include side effects such as sweating and abdominal pain, which need to be monitored. Its role in enhancing the eating ability of patients undergoing cancer treatment is vital, as it directly influences their nutritional intake and overall health. [Data: Entities (2283), Relationships (3102)]\n\n## Interrelationship between Nistatina and Pilocarpina\n\nBoth Nistatina and Pilocarpina are used to treat conditions related to mouth dryness and infections, highlighting their complementary roles in patient care. Their combined use can be particularly beneficial for patients experiencing xerostomia due to cancer treatments, as they address both the fungal infections and the dry mouth symptoms. This synergy can lead to improved patient outcomes, as managing both conditions simultaneously can enhance the patient's ability to eat and maintain nutritional status. [Data: Relationships (9492)]\n\n## Nutritional support alongside medication\n\nNistatina may be prescribed alongside nutritional support for patients with fungal infections, emphasizing the importance of a holistic approach to patient care. This relationship indicates that addressing fungal infections is not only about treating the infection itself but also about ensuring that patients can maintain adequate nutrition. The integration of nutritional support with antifungal treatment can significantly improve patient recovery and quality of life, particularly in those with compromised health due to cancer. [Da